				<h1 id="versionHeadLine" class="headline">

Candidate Information		</h1>
	
		<div id="cc5f8c90dc-b4cb-431b-90ee-10648f8df655" data-containerid="5f8c90dc-b4cb-431b-90ee-10648f8df655" class="pageContent cpGrid cpGrid24"  data-smoothscrolling="True">
			

		<div class="row outer wide"><!--
--><div class="outer col col24 first last" style="" data-widgetcontainerid="e3d12043-ccb5-499b-ad2f-fdb166acf951">				
	<div class="row nest first last wide">
	
	<div class="inner col col24 first last id7b72865f-6bf8-4e17-9993-cd4f212cecc1" style="" data-widgetcontainerid="7b72865f-6bf8-4e17-9993-cd4f212cecc1">	
<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditor8a70b32e-b54f-4e31-8237-15f583ae1bec" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <p>The City Clerk&apos;s Office is responsible for the conduct of municipal elections. We provide nomination packets and general guidelines to candidates interested in running for Mayor or City Council. &nbsp;</p><h2 aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pasted="true">Notice of Nomination Papers Issued</h2><p aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">This notice is posted in accordance with Elections Code &sect; 10224.5:&nbsp;</p><ul role="presentation"><li aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/16370" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Notice of Nomination Papers Issued</a></li></ul><p aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">The City Clerk has issued nomination papers to the incumbent for the office of Mayor. The office of Mayor is elected at large and Measure F, which was passed at the June 2, 2026 Special Municipal Election, did not affect an incumbent&rsquo;s eligibility to run for the open office of Mayor.&nbsp;</p><p data-pasted="true">Due to the passage of Measure F at the June 2, 2026 Special Municipal Election, the offices of City Council Districts 1, 2, 3, and 5 transitioned from at large elections to district elections. Accordingly, these offices have no eligible incumbents for the purposes of the incumbent filing provisions. &nbsp;</p><p>Nomination papers may be obtained and filed at City Hall, City Clerk&rsquo;s Office, 835 East 14<sup>th</sup> Street, San Leandro, between July 13, 2026 through August 7, 2026, between the hours of 8:30 a.m. and 5:00 p.m. If an incumbent eligible for re-election does not file nomination papers by the deadline, the filing deadline for that office is extended to Wednesday, August 12, 2026, for non-incumbent candidates only.</p><h2 class="subhead1" aria-level="2">Appointments Required</h2><p>Please contact us to schedule an appointment. Candidate filing is a multi-step process and may require more than one appointment. Below are common types of appointments and how long you can expect at each one:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Picking up paperwork to run for Mayor or City Council (60 minutes)</li><li>Dropping off paperwork to run for Mayor or City Council (60 minutes)</li><li>Meeting with the City Clerk or Deputy City Clerk (30 minutes)</li><li>Assistance with the City&apos;s electronic campaign filing system (30-45 minutes)</li></ul><h2 class="subhead1">Nomination Period and Candidate Filing Information&nbsp;</h2><p>During the Nomination Period, candidates can pick up and file paperwork to run for office. &nbsp;For the November 3, 2026 General Municipal Election, the nomination period opens on July 13, 2026, and closes at 5 p.m. on August 7, 2026 (unless extended).&nbsp;</p><p>If an eligible incumbent does not file nomination documents for re-election by the close of the nomination period on August 7, 2026, the nomination period for that office shall be extended to Wednesday, August 12, 2026, at 5:00 p.m. for non-incumbents only.</p><h2 class="subhead1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" aria-level="2">Filing Fee</h2><p aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" aria-level="2" data-pasted="true">There is no filing fee to run for office. A fee may apply if the candidate chooses to publish a Candidate Statement of Qualifications in the voter information guide.&nbsp;</p><h2 class="subhead1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">Preparing to Run for Office</h2><p>You can prepare to run for office by taking the following steps:&nbsp;</p><ol><li>Verify that your <a href="https://voterstatus.sos.ca.gov/">voter registration</a> is current</li><li>File a <a href="https://www.fppc.ca.gov/forms/">Form 501 (Candidate Intention Statement)</a> before raising or spending any money</li><li>File a <a href="https://www.sanleandro.org/201/Campaign-Signs">Declaration of Intent to Install Temporary Election Campaign Signs</a> (at least 2 days before installing any sign)</li><li>Review the <a href="https://www.fppc.ca.gov/learn/campaign-rules/candidate-toolkit/">FPPC Candidate Toolkit</a> to understand the rules for raising or spending money</li><li>Get <a href="https://www.fppc.ca.gov/learn/training-and-outreach/upcoming-training-opportunities/">candidate and treasurer training</a> from the Fair Political Practices Commission</li><li>Review important <a href="https://www.fppc.ca.gov/siteassets/documents/tad/filing_schedules/2026/2026_local_nov_01_cand_final.pdf" aria-describedby="audioeye_pdf_message">reporting deadlines</a> for campaign committees</li></ol><h2 class="subhead1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">Preparing for a Candidate Appointment</h2><p>The candidate will meet with the City Clerk or Deputy City Clerk. The first appointment begins with verifying the candidate&apos;s voter registration. The following documents will be issued to the candidate and reviewed:&nbsp;</p><ul><li><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/16109/Candidate-Information-Guide-2026">Candidate Information Guide</a></li><li>Nomination Paper</li><li>Declaration of Candidacy</li><li>Ballot Designation Worksheet</li><li>Candidate Statement of Qualifications</li><li>Code of Fair Campaign Practices</li><li>Declaration of Intent to Install Political Signs</li><li><a href="https://www.fppc.ca.gov/">FPPC Forms and Campaign Finance Deadlines</a><ul><li>Form 700</li><li>Form 501</li><li>Form 410</li><li>Form 460</li><li>Form 470 + Supplement</li><li>Form 497</li><li>Campaign Disclosure Manual 2</li></ul></li><li>Submittal Checklist</li><li><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/7367" rel="noopener" target="_blank" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Council Member District Map (PDF</a>)</li></ul><p>The City Clerk&apos;s Office maintains a roster of candidate information that is available to the public, media, and others. This roster is updated during the Nomination Period as forms are filed. At the return appointment, candidates will meet with the City Clerk or Deputy City Clerk to file the completed paperwork and take the Oath of Office.&nbsp;</p>
    </div>

